# rhwp glyph fit for why-hwp: draw a display substitute at the source face's widths.
# Base: rhwp 7213ed1f9 after the source edits in wasm/patch-rhwp.sh and every
# earlier wasm/patches/*.patch in name order; apply this after
# rhwp-zlayout3.patch.
# Zero-context diff (apply with git apply --unidiff-zero).
#
# When a document's face is not installed, the font environment maps it onto a
# supplied face for display only and keeps the missing face as the metric face
# (TextStyle::metric_font_family), so glyph origins are where the missing face
# puts them. The glyphs were drawn at the substitute's own widths, so their
# boxes in the PDF ended short or long: on Linux, 돋움체 `.` advances 0.5 em
# and the substitute draws it 0.27 em wide; 한컴 윤고딕 250 Hangul advances
# 0.9 em and HCR Dotum draws it 0.97 em wide.
#
# - svg.rs: a cluster of a TrueType slot whose drawn face is not its metric face
#   is fitted to its layout advance with textLength, as ASCII letters and digits
#   already are. Installed faces have no metric face and are drawn as before.
# - render_tree.rs: FootnoteMarkerNode carries the metric face of its run
#   (not serialized when absent); layout fills it, other constructors pass None.
# - svg.rs: a footnote marker whose face is such a substitute is drawn through
#   draw_text, so each character gets the substitute's family chain and is
#   fitted to the metric face's advance. It was one <text> naming the missing
#   face, which fell back to the default font at its natural widths.
# - svg/tests.rs covers both.
